## Project layout

```
MP2/lens/
├── .cursorrules
├── project_notes.md      # session memory — update often
├── decisions.md          # stable design choices
├── README.md
├── app.py                # Streamlit: Upload → Processing → Report
├── models.py
├── session_builder.py
├── synthesis.py
├── report_generator.py
├── query_engine.py
├── export.py
├── ingestion.py          # LAST
├── transcription.py, emotion_*.py, screen_analysis.py, language_analysis.py
├── fixtures/
├── scripts/run_pipeline_fixture.py
└── outputs/              # gitignored artifacts
```

`Path(__file__).resolve().parent` for paths. UTF-8 text I/O.

---

## Flexible inputs + confidence

Any combination per session: **video**, **audio**, **transcript**, **study context**.

- `InputCapabilities` on each session; analyzers **skip** missing channels.
- **Confidence** on signals, timeline events, clusters, and sessions (`high` / `medium` / `low` + scores).
- `multi_modal_convergence` only when **≥2 channels with data** agree on friction.
- Report must state what was **not** available per participant.

---

## Technology stack

| Layer | Tool |
|-------|------|
| Ingestion | moviepy, opencv (deferred) |
| Transcription | openai-whisper local |
| Vocal emotion | transformers wav2vec2 emotion model |
| Face + screen | GPT-4o vision (`OPENAI_API_KEY`) — 5s frames; cost estimate first |
| Language / report / query | Mistral via **HuggingFace Inference API** (`HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY`) — primary; rule-based fallback; other providers only via one env flag later |
| Clustering | chromadb + sentence-transformers (local fallback OK) |
| UI | streamlit → Streamlit Cloud |
| Export | fpdf2 |

---

## Build order

1. models → session_builder → synthesis → report_generator → query_engine → export → app  
2. fixtures + `scripts/run_pipeline_fixture.py`  
3. ingestion + modality extractors **only after** fixture pipeline approved  

---

## Generative UI + demo

- Report **structure** follows evidence (dominant cluster vs balanced).
- **Query UI** generates views from natural language.
- **June 3 demo:** transcript-only vs LENS on same p5.js session; list what text-only missed.

